while the world mourns the loss of a  prince tonight the las vegas community  honors the life of a hip-hop king  dmx passed away on friday after  suffering from a heart attack a week  earlier  tonight new era las vegas is holding a  vigil to celebrate one of rap's most  iconic voices madison kimbrough joins us  live from mlk and cary with more  madison yeah sasha the vigil is taking  place in front of the mlk statue that  you can see  right behind me it's meant to bring the  community together to honor an artist  that meant so much to so many  especially within the black community  people have started to gather in a meet  and greet setting where the rapper's  music will be played later on  followed by a ceremony later on where  those who want to speak  will share the impact the rapper had on  their lives flowers candles and prayer  will follow  dmx began his wrapping career in the  early 1990's  and released his debut album 23 years  ago that was in 1998  however throughout the years he had a  long struggle with drug addiction and  legal battles  that took center stage the host of the  event minister stretch  sander of new era las vegas shares his  thoughts on the artist's life and legacy  and what he means to him we can't grab a  musician we can't grab a leader and find  a perfect human being  right there's always going to be  something people can say well he was  this  he was that i think the dmx had a pure  heart i think that he meant well  a lot of the music of today has been  commercialized and so the music doesn't  speak to the conditions  well dmx was the last of that tribe he  was the last of those mohigans  who music they recorded music that  reflected the community  the rapper's family released a statement  where they said dmx whose birth name was  earl simmons  was a warrior who fought till the very  end he loved his family with all of his  heart and they cherished the times they  have spent with him  later on we hope to talk to more people  about what dmx meant to them  we got some people here even from  michigan that came all the way over to  las vegas  to celebrate his life we also hope to  show you more of the ceremony as it  takes place until seven o'clock  reporting live madison kimbrough 8 news  now
 

